{"path":"std/fs/fn.remove_dir_all.html","title":"Function remove_dir_all","description":"Removes a directory at this path, after removing all its contents. Use carefully!","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"main-content"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function remove_dir_all"}]},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0 · "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/std/fs.rs.html#3185-3187","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"pub fn remove_dir_all<P: AsRef<Path>>(path: P) -> Result<()>"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removes a directory at this path, after removing all its contents. Use carefully!"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function does "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" follow symbolic links and it will simply remove the symbolic link itself."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"platform-specific-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Platform-specific behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These implementation details "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/index.html#platform-specific-behavior","title":"mod std::io","children":[{"type":"text","value":"may change in the future"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"“Unix-like”: By default, this function currently corresponds to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"openat"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"fdopendir"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"unlinkat"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"lstat"},{"type":"text","value":" on Unix-family platforms, except where noted otherwise."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"“Windows”: This function currently corresponds to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"CreateFileW"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"GetFileInformationByHandleEx"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"SetFileInformationByHandle"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"NtCreateFile"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"time-of-check-to-time-of-use-toctou-race-conditions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Time-of-check to time-of-use (TOCTOU) race conditions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/index.html#time-of-check-to-time-of-use-toctou","title":"mod std::fs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"module-level TOCTOU explanation"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On most platforms, "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"fs::remove_dir_all"},{"type":"text","value":" protects against symlink TOCTOU races by default. However, on the following platforms, this protection is not provided and the function should not be used in security-sensitive contexts:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Miri"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Even when emulating targets where the underlying implementation will protect against TOCTOU races, Miri will not do so."}]},{"children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"QNX"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Redox OS"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"VxWorks"}]},{"type":"text","value":": This function does not protect against TOCTOU races, as the underlying platform does not implement the required platform support to do so."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/fn.remove_file.html","title":"fn std::fs::remove_file","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"fs::remove_file"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/fn.remove_dir.html","title":"fn std::fs::remove_dir","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"fs::remove_dir"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/fn.remove_dir_all.html","title":"fn std::fs::remove_dir_all","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"remove_dir_all"}]},{"type":"text","value":" will fail if "},{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/fn.remove_dir.html","title":"fn std::fs::remove_dir","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"remove_dir"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/fn.remove_file.html","title":"fn std::fs::remove_file","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"remove_file"}]},{"type":"text","value":" fail on "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"any"}]},{"type":"text","value":" constituent paths, "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"including"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the root "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"path"},{"type":"text","value":". Consequently,"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The directory you are deleting "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"must"}]},{"type":"text","value":" exist, meaning that this function is "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not idempotent"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/fn.remove_dir_all.html","title":"fn std::fs::remove_dir_all","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"remove_dir_all"}]},{"type":"text","value":" will fail if the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"path"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" a directory."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consider ignoring the error if validating the removal is not required for your use case."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function may return "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/enum.ErrorKind.html#variant.DirectoryNotEmpty","title":"variant std::io::ErrorKind::DirectoryNotEmpty","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"io::ErrorKind::DirectoryNotEmpty"}]},{"type":"text","value":" if the directory is concurrently written into, which typically indicates some contents were removed but not all. "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/enum.ErrorKind.html#variant.NotFound","title":"variant std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"io::ErrorKind::NotFound"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is only returned if no removal occurs."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"use std::fs;\n\nfn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {\n    fs::remove_dir_all(\"/some/dir\")?;\n    Ok(())\n}"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0Ause+std::fs;%0A%0Afn+main()+-%3E+std::io::Result%3C()%3E+%7B%0A++++fs::remove_dir_all(%22/some/dir%22)?;%0A++++Ok(())%0A%7D&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]}]}}
